cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MESH: connectome-scale contact detection and EM proofreading for putative gap junctions"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
# TODO before release: confirm the author list, add ORCIDs, and add co-authors
# / the Fenk Lab affiliation as appropriate for the paper.
authors:
  - family-names: Serbe
    given-names: Etienne
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ETigerschuss/MESH"
abstract: >-
  MESH detects physical appositions between neurons reconstructed in the FlyWire
  connectome of the FAFB electron-microscopy volume, and supports their manual
  validation in EM. Contacts are found geometrically (k-d tree over mesh
  vertices, 100 nm proximity), grouped into discrete sites, confined to genuine
  membrane apposition by segmentation adjacency, and rendered as EM image stacks
  in an interactive viewer where an expert can measure, accept or reject each
  site. Because chemical synapses are annotated in FlyWire but gap junctions are
  not, subtracting annotated chemical synapses from validated appositions yields
  a ranked list of putative electrical-synapse sites.
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila
  - FlyWire
  - FAFB
  - electron microscopy
  - gap junctions
  - electrical synapses
license: MIT
